    "paths": {
      "/openai/v1/responses": {
        "post": {
          "summary": "DeepSeek V4.1 Flash",
          "deprecated": false,
          "description": ":::warning\n**⚠️ Chat only**\n\nThis model currently supports chat requests only and has not yet been adapted for agent use. Connecting it to an agent may cause request errors or unexpected results.\n:::\n\n> DeepSeek V4.1 Flash API is an OpenAI Responses–compatible endpoint that accepts a plain string or a structured input array, thinks deeply by default, and supports function calling, image understanding, and structured JSON output.\n\n<CardGroup cols={2}>\n  <Card title=\"Thinking Control\" icon=\"🧠\">\n    Deep thinking is on by default, with seven effort levels to tune.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Multimodal Input\" icon=\"🖼️\">\n    Supports mixed text and image inputs in a single message.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Tools & Structured Output\" icon=\"✨\">\n    Custom function calling, and answers constrained to JSON.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Unified Endpoint\" icon=\"💻\">\n    Uses the unified <code>/openai/v1/responses</code> endpoint with <code>model</code> set to <code>deepseek-v4-1-flash</code>.\n  </Card>\n</CardGroup>\n\n## Thinking\n\nThe model **thinks by default**. Turn it off for a faster and cheaper answer — `reasoning.effort` and `thinking.type` do the same job, so you only need one of them.\n\n:::caution\n`max_output_tokens`, `temperature` and `top_p` are **not supported** on this model and have no effect.\n:::\n\n<AccordionGroup>\n  <Accordion title=\"Turn thinking off\">\n    These two are equivalent:\n\n    ```json\n    { \"reasoning\": { \"effort\": \"none\" } }\n    ```\n\n    ```json\n    { \"thinking\": { \"type\": \"disabled\" } }\n    ```\n\n    `thinking.type`: `enabled` (default) or `disabled`.\n  </Accordion>\n\n  <Accordion title=\"Effort levels\">\n    `reasoning.effort` accepts `none`, `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh` and `max`.\n\n    `none` turns thinking off (same as `thinking.type: \"disabled\"`). `minimal` keeps thinking brief. Above that, the higher the level the more thoroughly the model thinks and the more tokens it spends.\n  </Accordion>\n</AccordionGroup>\n\n## Tools & input\n\n<AccordionGroup>\n  <Accordion title=\"Function calling\">\n    Declare the functions the model may call. Only the `function` type is supported:\n\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"tools\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"function\",\n          \"name\": \"get_current_weather\",\n          \"description\": \"Get the current weather in a given location\",\n          \"parameters\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"location\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"description\": \"The city and state, e.g. San Francisco, CA\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\"location\"]\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"tool_choice\": \"auto\"\n    }\n    ```\n\n    `tool_choice` defaults to `auto` once `tools` is present. Use `required` to force a call, or `{\"type\": \"function\", \"name\": \"...\"}` to pin one specific function.\n  </Accordion>\n\n  <Accordion title=\"Return the execution result\">\n    The model answers with a `function_call` item. Run the function, then append both that item and your `function_call_output` to `input` — the two are paired through `call_id`:\n\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"input\": [\n        { \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"What's the weather in Beijing today?\" },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"function_call\",\n          \"call_id\": \"call_00_xxx\",\n          \"name\": \"get_current_weather\",\n          \"arguments\": \"{\\\"location\\\":\\\"Beijing\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"function_call_output\",\n          \"call_id\": \"call_00_xxx\",\n          \"output\": \"Sunny, 25°C\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n    ```\n  </Accordion>\n\n  <Accordion title=\"Image understanding\">\n    Mix `input_image` and `input_text` parts inside one message. `image_url` takes a publicly reachable URL or a `data:image/{format};base64,{encoded}` string:\n\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"input\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"user\",\n          \"content\": [\n            { \"type\": \"input_image\", \"image_url\": \"https://example.com/demo.png\" },\n            { \"type\": \"input_text\", \"text\": \"What is in this image?\" }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n    ```\n  </Accordion>\n\n  <Accordion title=\"JSON output\">\n    Set `text.format` to constrain the answer to JSON:\n\n    ```json\n    { \"text\": { \"format\": { \"type\": \"json_object\" } } }\n    ```\n\n    Use `json_schema` instead to validate the answer against a schema of your own.\n  </Accordion>\n</AccordionGroup>\n\n## Error handling\n\nCheck the response body, not only the HTTP status. Errors are returned either as `{\"code\": ..., \"msg\": \"...\"}` (for example 401 invalid API key, 402 insufficient credits, 429 rate limited; the HTTP status may still be 200) or as `{\"error\": {\"type\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}}`.\n",
          "operationId": "openai/v1/responses",
          "tags": [],
          "parameters": [],
          "requestBody": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "model": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "Target model name. Allowed values: `deepseek-v4-1-flash`.",
                      "enum": [
                        "deepseek-v4-1-flash"
                      ],
                      "examples": [
                        "deepseek-v4-1-flash"
                      ]
                    },
                    "stream": {
                      "type": "boolean",
                      "description": "When true, responses stream in real time as server-sent events. When false, the full response is returned at once after completion. Default is true.",
                      "default": true
                    },
                    "input": {
                      "oneOf": [
                        {
                          "type": "string",
                          "description": "Input can be a string."
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "array",
                          "description": "Input can be an array; each element is a message, a function call, or a function call result.",
                          "items": {
                            "oneOf": [
                              {
                                "type": "object",
                                "title": "message",
                                "description": "A message object with role and content. `type` may be omitted, in which case it defaults to `message`.",
                                "properties": {
                                  "type": {
                                    "type": "string",
                                    "enum": [
                                      "message"
                                    ]
                                  },
                                  "role": {
                                    "type": "string",
                                    "description": "The role of the message author. `system` and `developer` instructions take precedence over `user`, while `assistant` carries a previous answer.",
                                    "enum": [
                                      "system",
                                      "developer",
                                      "user",
                                      "assistant"
                                    ]
                                  },
                                  "content": {
                                    "oneOf": [
                                      {
                                        "type": "string"
                                      },
                                      {
                                        "type": "array",
                                        "items": {
                                          "oneOf": [
                                            {
                                              "type": "object",
                                              "title": "input_text",
                                              "properties": {
                                                "type": {
                                                  "type": "string",
                                                  "enum": [
                                                    "input_text"
                                                  ]
                                                },
                                                "text": {
                                                  "type": "string",
                                                  "description": "Text content."
                                                }
                                              },
                                              "required": [
                                                "type",
                                                "text"
                                              ]
                                            },
                                            {
                                              "type": "object",
                                              "title": "input_image",
                                              "properties": {
                                                "type": {
                                                  "type": "string",
                                                  "enum": [
                                                    "input_image"
                                                  ]
                                                },
                                                "image_url": {
                                                  "type": "string",
                                                  "description": "Image address. A publicly reachable URL, or a `data:image/{format};base64,{encoded}` string."
                                                },
                                                "detail": {
                                                  "type": "string",
                                                  "description": "Image understanding precision. Higher values provide more detail but may increase latency.",
                                                  "enum": [
                                                    "auto",
                                                    "low",
                                                    "high",
                                                    "xhigh"
                                                  ]
                                                }
                                              },
                                              "required": [
                                                "type",
                                                "image_url"
                                              ]
                                            },
                                            {
                                              "type": "object",
                                              "title": "output_text",
                                              "description": "An assistant answer replayed in a multi-turn conversation.",
                                              "properties": {
                                                "type": {
                                                  "type": "string",
                                                  "enum": [
                                                    "output_text"
                                                  ]
                                                },
                                                "text": {
                                                  "type": "string",
                                                  "description": "Text content."
                                                }
                                              },
                                              "required": [
                                                "type",
                                                "text"
                                              ]
                                            }
                                          ]
                                        }
                                      }
                                    ],
                                    "description": "Message content. Either a plain string, or an array of text and image parts."
                                  }
                                },
                                "required": [
                                  "role",
                                  "content"
                                ]
                              },
                              {
                                "type": "object",
                                "title": "function_call",
                                "description": "A function call the model made in a previous turn. Paired with `function_call_output` through `call_id`.",
                                "properties": {
                                  "type": {
                                    "type": "string",
                                    "enum": [
                                      "function_call"
                                    ]
                                  },
                                  "call_id": {
                                    "type": "string",
                                    "description": "Call identifier. Pass back the `call_id` from the previous output verbatim."
                                  },
                                  "name": {
                                    "type": "string",
                                    "description": "Name of the function the model called."
                                  },
                                  "arguments": {
                                    "type": "string",
                                    "description": "Function arguments, as a JSON string."
                                  }
                                },
                                "required": [
                                  "type",
                                  "call_id",
                                  "name",
                                  "arguments"
                                ]
                              },
                              {
                                "type": "object",
                                "title": "function_call_output",
                                "description": "The result of running a function, returned to the model.",
                                "properties": {
                                  "type": {
                                    "type": "string",
                                    "enum": [
                                      "function_call_output"
                                    ]
                                  },
                                  "call_id": {
                                    "type": "string",
                                    "description": "Call identifier. Must match the `call_id` of the corresponding `function_call`."
                                  },
                                  "output": {
                                    "type": "string",
                                    "description": "Function execution result, as text."
                                  }
                                },
                                "required": [
                                  "type",
                                  "call_id",
                                  "output"
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          "minItems": 1
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    "instructions": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "System instructions for the model, inserted as a system message ahead of `input`."
                    },
                    "reasoning": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "description": "Reasoning configuration for the model.",
                      "properties": {
                        "effort": {
                          "type": "string",
                          "description": "Reasoning effort level. Higher values provide more thorough reasoning but may increase latency. `none` turns thinking off (same as `thinking.type: \"disabled\"`). `minimal` keeps thinking brief. Defaults to reasoning being enabled.",
                          "enum": [
                            "none",
                            "minimal",
                            "low",
                            "medium",
                            "high",
                            "xhigh",
                            "max"
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    "thinking": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "description": "Thinking configuration. An alternative to `reasoning.effort` — configure either one, not both.",
                      "properties": {
                        "type": {
                          "type": "string",
                          "description": "Thinking behavior: `enabled` (default) or `disabled`.",
                          "enum": [
                            "enabled",
                            "disabled"
                          ],
                          "default": "enabled"
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    "tools": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "description": "Optional tools that the model may call. Only the `function` type is supported.",
                      "items": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                          "type": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Tool type. Fixed as `function`.",
                            "enum": [
                              "function"
                            ]
                          },
                          "name": {
                            "type": "string",
